# HUMAN DECISION REQUIRED (NXP-FIRMWARE-EULA). Never merge by hand.
#
# scripts/build/configure_buildroot.sh appends these lines to a FRDM .config
# only when config/boards/frdm-imx8mp.env sets
# BHP_BOARD_NXP_FIRMWARE_EULA=accepted-adr-NNNN and ADR NNNN is accepted and
# carries the <!-- @canonical nxp-firmware-eula-acceptance --> marker. A human
# makes and records that decision; an agent never does. Selecting them makes
# Buildroot download NXP's self-extracting firmware-imx archive, run it with
# --auto-accept, and install NXP-licensed IW612 firmware: that is accepting the
# NXP Software License Agreement on the user's behalf.
#
# firmware-imx supplies the LPDDR4 training firmware (ddr_fw.bin) without which
# imx8-boot-sd.bin, and therefore sdcard.img, cannot be produced.
#
# ADR 0016 (accepted 2026-11-10) covers firmware-imx under v58. It does not
# cover the IW612 firmware at bhp-nxp-iw612-firmware's pinned tag
# (lf-6.12.49-2.2.0, licence v63), so BR2_PACKAGE_BHP_NXP_IW612_FIRMWARE stays
# unselected until the owner accepts v63 or the package is re-pinned.
BR2_PACKAGE_FIRMWARE_IMX=y
BR2_PACKAGE_FIRMWARE_IMX_LPDDR4=y
